          "case_name": "Interest of M.S. & K.S.",
          "citation": "2014 S.D. 17, 845 N.W.2d 366",
          "court": "South Dakota Supreme Court",
          "year": 2014,
          "date_decided": "2014-04-02",
          "holding": "The court affirmed termination, holding the circuit court did not clearly err in finding that further reasonable efforts would be futile and that statutory good cause under SDCL 26-8A-21.1 and 26-8A-26.1 justified terminating the parents' rights.",
          "relevance": "It shows how a front-end, services-based response can be exhausted and converted into a petition when the underlying risk persists.",
          "quote": "the court had sufficient evidence and reasoning to find Mother's efforts futile when considering the children's best interests",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/2713909/interest-of-ms-ks/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 2713909
        },
        {
          "case_name": "Cotton v. Stange",
          "citation": "1998 S.D. 81, 582 N.W.2d 25",
          "court": "South Dakota Supreme Court",
          "year": 1998,
          "date_decided": "1998-07-22",
          "holding": "The court reversed the denial of summary judgment and ordered judgment for two DSS social workers, holding they were immune under SDCL 26-8A-14 because the children produced only evidence of negligent investigation, not of bad faith.",
          "relevance": "Where the agency chooses in-home monitoring over removal, this case holds that choice is protected unless made in bad faith.",
          "quote": "These circumstances might amount to negligence but they do not equate with bad faith.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/900289/cotton-v-stange/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 900289
        },
        {
          "case_name": "People ex rel. J.S.B., Jr.",
          "citation": "2005 S.D. 3, 691 N.W.2d 611",
          "court": "South Dakota Supreme Court",
          "year": 2005,
          "date_decided": "2005-01-05",
          "holding": "The court held that ASFA's aggravated-circumstances exception to reasonable efforts does not override ICWA's active efforts requirement, but affirmed termination because DSS in fact continued to provide active efforts that proved unsuccessful.",
          "relevance": "The mutual Family Service Agreement the court accepted as active efforts is the model for a services-first, non-punitive response.",
          "quote": "Under ICWA, DSS was bound by law to make \"active efforts\" to reunite J.S.B with his father, but it was not required to persist with futile efforts.",
          "url": "https://www.courtlistener.com/opinion/901424/the-people-of-the-state-of-south-dakota-in-the-interest-of-jsb-jr/",
          "courtlistener_cluster_id": 901424
        }
